VS Code extension that live-previews Shattered Archive DSL color codes ({R, {G, {x, ...) in a side-by-side webview as the user types in any editor tab. Standalone package (not built with Vite/the app dev-server scripts like the other apps/* clients) — bundled with esbuild into a single dist/extension.js and either run via the Extension Development Host (F5) or packaged into a .vsix with vsce. The color renderer (src/renderDslToHtml.ts) is a deliberate hand-synced copy of game-client's renderDslColorPreviewHtml.ts, since a VSIX can't import across the workspace at runtime. src/ansi.ts and src/convert.ts add ANSI .txt support (format auto-detected per file: any ESC[ means ANSI, else DSL) and the Copy as Plain/ANSI Text commands; ansi.ts is a hand-synced copy of dsl-log-preview/src/ansiToHtml.ts plus game-client dsl-to-ansi.ts. The CSI matcher deliberately tolerates CR/LF inside a sequence because the real GameLog-*.txt files wrap lines mid-escape (ESC[1;31<CRLF>m).
